; MAP for the input format: n, k, then a_11, a_21, ..., a_k1, a_12, ..., a_kn.
; Example function: f(x_1, ..., x_k) = x_1 + ... + x_k.
; R11 = number of tuples remaining; R12 = k.
; R2-R5 = parameters to F; F leaves them unchanged and returns the result in R0.

Read 11
Read 12

MAP_LOOP:
; Clear all parameter cells so unused parameters are zero.
Load =0
Store 2
Store 3
Store 4
Store 5

; Read exactly k values into R2, ..., R(k+1).
Load 12
Sub =1
JZero READ_K1
Load 12
Sub =2
JZero READ_K2
Load 12
Sub =3
JZero READ_K3
Jump READ_K4

READ_K1:
Read 2
Jump APPLY_F

READ_K2:
Read 2
Read 3
Jump APPLY_F

READ_K3:
Read 2
Read 3
Read 4
Jump APPLY_F

READ_K4:
Read 2
Read 3
Read 4
Read 5

APPLY_F:
call F
Write 0
Load 11
Sub =1
Store 11
JZero END
Jump MAP_LOOP

; Example f: sum of the first k parameters.
; Uses only volatile cells and R0 for the result, preserving R2-R5.
F:
Load 12
Sub =1
JZero F_K1
Load 12
Sub =2
JZero F_K2
Load 12
Sub =3
JZero F_K3

F_K4:
Load 2
Add 3
Add 4
Add 5
Store 0
ret

F_K1:
Load 2
Store 0
ret

F_K2:
Load 2
Add 3
Store 0
ret

F_K3:
Load 2
Add 3
Add 4
Store 0
ret

END:
Halt 0
